  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n\nCOMPOUND VERB:\n{書|か}く (to write) + {殴|なぐ}る (to hit/strike)\nThe {殴|なぐ}る component suggests violent, careless motion.\n\nNUANCE:\nImplies writing that is:\n- Hasty and careless\n- Often illegible or messy\n- Sometimes done emotionally (in anger, frustration)\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {丁寧|ていねい}に{書|か}く (to write carefully)\n- {清書|せいしょ}する (to make a fair copy)\n\nRELATED:\n- {走|はし}り{書|が}き (hasty writing)\n- {乱筆|らんぴつ} (poor handwriting)\n- {殴|なぐ}り{書|が}き (scribble, scrawl)",
